{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Grew fat.</b> A term of fatness." "<b>Covered.</b> Like כָּסִיתָ — a term as in ״כִּי כִסָּה פָנָיו בְּחֶלְבּוֹ״ (Job 15) — like a person who is fat on the inside and his flanks fold over on the outside. And so it says (ibid.) ״וַיַּעַשׂ פִּימָה עֲלֵי כָסֶל״." "<b>Covered.</b> There is a [form in the]piel in the language of covering, as in ״וְכֹסֶה קָלוֹן עָרוּם״ (Proverbs 12). And if he had written כִשִּׂיתָ, with a dagesh, it would have sounded like 'you covered others,' as in ״כִּי כִסָּה פָנָיו״ (Job 15)." "<b>And he spurned the Rock of his salvation.</b> He denied Him and despised Him, as it says (Ezekiel 8) ״אֲחוֹרֵיהֶם אֶל הֵיכַל ה׳ וגו׳״ — there is no greater act of spurning than this (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:17.167914482Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}